{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore /srv/inventory/data/config.json from the latest backup in /var/backups/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The backup directory contained one backup, inventory-20260901.tar.gz. Its config.json was valid JSON with SHA-256 1448a747..., and the restored target directly matched that checksum before and after reboot; the prepared damaged checksum had differed.","evidence_ids":["prepared-restore-data","cmd-1b8122728c5644e9","cmd-5db15b0d926e4283","cmd-61fae48718334f01","cmd-c5c1d6c7ea304a05"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve all other current inventory files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initial inventory contained only config.json and current.txt. current.txt retained its SHA-256, mode, ownership, size, and mtime across the restoration, and its checksum remained unchanged after reboot. No restore staging entries remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1b8122728c5644e9","cmd-35012c0e65e840ab","cmd-61fae48718334f01","cmd-c5c1d6c7ea304a05"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The atomic target replacement and temporary staging directory were necessary for the restore, and staging was removed (cmd-61fae48718334f01). The scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol and completed successfully (cmd-38857eb74a6e41b2). Other timeline commands were read-only checks or expected connection failures during reboot. There was no executor-caused residue, package damage, new failed service, or unsafe exposure; ssh.service was already failed before preparation and remained so afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-61fae48718334f01","cmd-38857eb74a6e41b2","cmd-c5c1d6c7ea304a05","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both public task outcomes are satisfied with direct before-and-after evidence. The node-restart protocol includes a pre-restart boot identity and relevant healthy filesystem, network, backup, and data state; restart acknowledgement; observed interruption; a different post-restart identity; and recovered services and persistent data. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Node-wide systemd state was degraded because ssh.service was failed before preparation and after execution. This was pre-existing and did not affect the demonstrated inventory restore, but prevents claiming wholly clean system-wide service health during the restart protocol.","No inventory-specific or cluster service existed, so restart recovery evidence appropriately covers the applicable filesystem, network, backup, and data state rather than an application or cluster service."]}
